sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-11> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Very few living species will leave descendants in the far future, and those that will prevail and give rise to new dominant species will be the common, widespread species of the larger, dominant groups.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Few living species will leave descendants; common species of dominant groups will prevail";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter XIV, “Recapitulation and Conclusion”; section “Concluding remarks”. Scope: living species and their future descendants (testable retrospectively in the fossil record)"
}
